Max change log (1997)
=====================

VERSION HISTORY
---------------
12/18/97 Max 2.1
	Selection and most commands working again.
	DRC/Extractor still broken.	
	.max read/write still loses timestamps/bboxes.

11/26/97 Max 2.0
	First limping start at new consistency mechanism in work.
	Does (quick) gds read of Rendition examples.
	DRC disabled.  Most everything else broken!

11/4/97 Max 1.31
	Fixed bugs in Max Manual.
	Fixed spelling of "apropos" in "Text Commands" window. :-)
	Fixed palette code so it doesn't break when 1 micron is not multiple of design grid.
	Fixed intermittent failure of max restart (when "colormap -new" required). 
	Lee fixed another wiring tool one off bug.
	Modified "quit" dialog to truncate excessively long lists of modified cells.
	Added "-source" option to db_cell_copy
	Fixed clipboard flakiness.
	Modified edit stack code to restore original box and window framing on pop.

10/31/97 Max 1.30
	Made g35 default tech.
	Added "Max Tutorial" button to Help menu.
	Slight update of Max Manual.
	Added Irsim to release.

10/23/97 Max 1.29
	"sel_what cells" augmented to give transform from instance coords to
	root coords.  (Also bbox now returned as list!)

	"orientation" takes transform returned by "sel_what cells" and returns
	orientation (e.g. r90 or fx)

10/21/97 Max 1.28
	Fixed label cmd to properly toggle between "box" and "point" type labels.
	Add generic 0.35 technology (g35)

10/17/97 Max 1.27
	Lee fixed a couple of minor bugs in the wiring tool.
	Fixed label command to allow "[]" in label.

10/13/97 Max 1.26
	fixed "clipboard paste" bug.
 
10/6/97 Max 1.25
	CHANGED ZOOM AGAIN:
	changed "z" back to "Zoom to Region"
	removed "Cntl-z" binding
	addded "t" for "Zoom In on Cursor"

10/1/97 Max 1.24
	CHANGED ZOOM COMMANDS SLIGHTLY:
		z      = zoom in on cursor
		Cntl-z = zoom to region (drag box zoom)
	updated max manual
	fixed pan_enable/pan_disable to nest
	disabled recursive drag box zoom, and grid move 
		(also disabled when button already down)
	
9/30/97 Max 1.23
	changed system path to:
		~/max_private/max
		$MMI_TOOLS/../mmi_local/max
		$MMI_TOOLS/max<version>
	implemented auto panning.
	changed view commands so cursor left pointing to same place in database
	implmented view commands (grid/view/zoom/center) for all modes.
	lay_point options changed: 
		rmed -no_default
		added: -no_clip and -warp
	added mn_button_state  (tells which mouse buttons are down)
	

9/11/97 Max 1.22
	added plotps style to scmos to permit "Max" layer printing with plotps
	fixed permissions in scmos/src dir :)
	latest and greatest scmos.plotps_* from Mark.
	print:  now setting cursor correctly, using temp files in /tmp,
		running plotps in background, and cleaning up after ourselves,
		added updates after dialog box, so box goes away even when
		print stuff takes its time.
	rmed gdsplot from default PRINT(types) (File/"Print Setup" menu), coded
		menu_add_print_type to allow Lee to add "gdsplot" back in :)
	included Lee's bug fix for wiring in Scmos (turds to the right problem)
		
9/10/97 Max 1.21
	fixed ":cif write" for ostyles with reducer specified.
	fixed rounding bugs in ":cif write"
	rmed "PROPRIETARY AND CONFIDENTIAL" on startup.
	converted tech variation separator from "_" to "-" for compatibility
		with MOSIS scmos.
	updated scmos tech to Magic Version 6.5, MOSIS version 8.2.8
		including tech variations.
	added scmos.plotps_pat and scmos.plops_pro (from Mark)
	fixed error msg when tech files not found.
	modified "cif_layers" to identify temp layers.
	fixed Mask menu to correctly determine temp layers.
	print (plotps) - cleaned up and fixed a number of bugs. (more work to do)
	
9/5/97  Max 1.20
	tweaked Copyright notice.  :)
	fixed two bugs in selection code that were breaking the wiring tool
		for scmos (problem involved multi-groups and multi-types on 
		plane simultaneously)
	incorporated Lee's one line change to misc.tcl
	removed hard coding of cif ostyle from print_plotps:
		if a tech needs special ostyle, add line to (e.g. tsmc.tcl):
		set PRINT(plotps,ostyle) "cif(10x)"
		I did this for tsmc.

9/2/97  Max 1.19
	removed DEBUG statements :)
	demoted some "errors" to warnings during GDSII read in.
	further restricted "info" command so can't go fishing for commands
		or global variables.
	modified init.tcl to tolerate restrictions on "info" command
	restricted "proc" and "rename" commands to not allow redefinition of
		"proc" (or "rename") - to plug security hole.
	created library of tclmods including MMI versions
		of "info", "rename" and "proc", so code can be shared
		by Max, Sue and Nst.
	incorporated Lee's latest changes to wire.tcl misc.tcl menu_bar.tcl

8/27/97 Max 1.18
	fixed code that determines toplevel cell when gds loaded.
	fixed initialization sequence so that CELL(gds_suffix) set in .maxrc
		works for reading files on command line.
	rmed "GDS-II reading is undoable" msg.
	fixed cif bug in outputting of instance transforms.
	
8/24/97 Max 1.17
	Using new license manager.
	Separate license capability (maxDev) now required for developer mode.
	Max tcl code now integral to executable (and encrypted).
	Tcl "info" command restricted, to discourage extraction of tcl code.
	Default gds suffix now user settable:  $CELL(gds_suffix) 
	Added appropriate updates after undo (e.g. title bar)
	Demoted various annoying warnings to info messages.
	Eliminated Cascaded menus for File/Import and File/Export.
	Modified File/"Import GDSII" to load toplevel cell into window.
	Can now load gds files on Max command line (need to have appropriate
		extension).
	User can now turn off display of instance names and ports via new
		palette entries:  iName and iPorts.
	
8/11/97 Max 1.16
	Help/Manual "completed" for now.
	Help/"MMI Documentation Guide" added.
	"Write lef" added to File/Export (Lee)
	Wiring tool now can snap to (per layer) channels (Lee)
	Added sel_region tcl command.
	Labels now default to points (Lee & mha)
	"Copy Cell Buffer" moved from File to Edit Menu.
	Can now create copy that shadows file (Lee)
	"Rename Cell Buffer" command added (to Edit Menu).
	Fixed FSBox.tcl (File Box) to properly initialize 
	  to given directory and file.

8/3/97  Max 1.15
	inverted bindings on "Internals, Show Area" and "Internals, Show Selected"
	moved Push/Pop/Edit In Place from Edit to View menu
	removed hot key from print 
	changed "Cntl" to "Ctrl" in Hot Key pretty printing.
	"Hot Keys" Help now documents Ctrl-BUT-2 in Main mode.
	"Hot Keys" Help in Label mode fixed. 
	":extract length" command restored.

7/24/97 Max 1.14
	Changed palette so buttons over layer name and layout sample are consistent:
	   BUT-1 toggles layer on/off
	   BUT-3 paints
	   Cntl-BUT-3 erases.
	Changed exit dialog to default to "Cancel"
	Made commands typed into controlling terminal bonafide max commands.
	Changed pretty printing of bindings as per Lee's and Mark's preferences.
	Fixed "Label Box" to update on "Done"
	Fixed bugs in clipboard functions.
	Added "-point x y" option to sel_net
	Added "Resource Tcl File" to Developer menu (to reload a maxtcl/ file)
	Converted from "hidden" list to "user" list for Help/"Text Commands"
	Implemented lay_styles allows dynamic control over display styles.

7/16/97 Max 1.13
	"Micromagic" -> "Micro Magic"
	added db_largest_box (for Lee's RC extractor)

7/11/97 Max 1.12
	Help/"Text Commands" now simplified, and supports "hiding" of commands
		from end-user.
	Help/"Hot Keys: much improved.
	Hot Keys in Menus new pretty printed.
	Auto restarts if new colormap required.

7/2/97 Max 1.11
	db_next_edge and db_next_distance now look down into instances
	db_next_edge and db_next_distance now take a tiletype rather than a plane
		as arg.
7/1/97 Max 1.10
	db_next_edge and db_next_distance augmented to allow limits on search.
	Max now permits exponential notation on input of coordinates and distances.

6/30/97 Max 1.9
	problem with Mask menu tracking cif_ostyle fixed.
	cif_ostyle fixed to reset units properly.
	gds output of degenerate rectangles fixed.
	tsmc_new.tech modified to avoid round off problems.
	next_distance left/right confusion when heading South fixed.

6/26/97 Max 1.8
	New tcl command cif_ostyle.
	Modified print_cifplot to proerply restore ostyle on exit.
	Implemented File/Import/"Read GDSII" menu item.
	Moved Misc/"Command List" to Help/"Tcl Commands"
	Created Developer menu (TODO:  don't display this for "normal" users)
	Implemented "units" statement for cif output that can set
	  resolution of database, "cif" plane, CIF output and GDS output, to
	  floating point number (microns).
	Added tcl var MN_UNITS_CHECK to control whether checking for off grid
	  numbers when converting user units (microns) to database units.
	Created tsmc_new tech file with new cif output style "tfab", for generating
	test chip.
	Created tsmc_tview tech file, for viewing final test chip GDS.
	
6/19/97 Max 1.7
	Fixes redisplay problem introduced in Max1.6
	GDS write of polygons implemented
	Outline styles and crosses implemented for display of polygons, i.e.
		45 contacts look ok now.
	Gds read of polygons fixed to not duplicate initial vertice at end.
	File/Print no longer changes resolution (resets ostyle)

6/9/97 Max 1.6
	Label Erase no longer leaves "turds" around.
	New selection commands (intended to eventually replace :select):
		sel_area
        	sel_chunk
		sel_cells (incomplete)
		sel_clear
		sel_save
	Implemented arbitrary angle off-grid (floating point) polygons:
		CHECK OUT "Misc/Test Polygon" menu button.
		db_polygon creates/deletes/lists polygons
		polygons read and written to .max files
		read on ":calma read" of non manhattan data (on layers
		having a directly associated max layer via "label" statements
		in cif input section of tech file)
		two point "polygons" are OVALS filling the manhattan
		bounding box defined by the two points. - ovals are used
		for corners in wire paths (below).

		writing of polygons to gds not yet implemented.
		polygons also not yet read/written to cif
	Implemented arbitrary angle wire paths 
		paths are defined by width and center-line
		CHECK OUT "Misc/Test Wire Path" menu button.
		db_wire_path creates/deletes/lists wire paths
		wire paths are read and written to .max files

		currently wire paths are not read/written from/to gds or cif files.
	Implemented gds_dump command to convert gds files to ascii format.

5/7/97 Max 1.5
	Label related menu items revamped:
		removed: Edit/Edit Label, Edit/Resize Label
		added: Edit/Add Label Edit/Edit Properties
	Control-C for dialog boxes fixed.

5/5/97 Max 1.4
	New menu command Edit/Extend (bound to Cntl-arrows) added.  This
		does magic "fill", i.e. it extends paint across box from
		edge to opposite edge, in direction indicated.
	New long command: lay_internals (obsoletes :expand, :unexpand)
	sel_what_cells now gives expand/unexpand info.
	Menu commands "View/Internals ..." fixed:  user now has
		choice of expanding/unexpanding selected 
		(does not effect descendents of selected) 
		or expanding/unexpanding an area (all the way down to paint).
	edit in place now expands new edit cell.
	Now changes to "wait" cursor during dialogs.
	menu help fixed and "help messages" reviewed and improved.
	Now posts help msgs ("? ...") for all dialogs
	All main mode bindings now in menu, and	obsolete bindings removed.

4/22/97	Max 1.3
	implemented "About Max"
	mode message now restored after browsing menus, also temporary mode
		message set during dialogs.
	rmed :grid command (obsoleted by lay_grid)
	db_cell_rename now takes old name arg.
	db_cell_file_tech command added (returns files technology)
	added check for correct tech to cell_load (so don't leave
		buffer around on failed load attempt).
	Fixed coredump due to background drc referencig deleted cell.
	removed interrogative from :flush (elevated to tk code for
		"Revert To Last Saved" 
	Removed interrogative on out of memory abort.

4/8/97-4/11/97  Max 1.2
	Implemented C and TCL primitives for finding edges and changes in
	"width".  (Useful for parastic extraction, routers, etc.)
	C routines:  DBNextEdge() DBNextDistance()
	Tcl procs:   db_next_edge db_next_distance
	For testing see menu item:  misc/"Test next_edge"
	menu_tool_cmd allows tool menu to be built from .maxrc
	db_cell_delete modified to support Lees Clipboard commands:
		 takes cell argument,
		 no longer does undo_flush or ":select clear"
	undo_flush command added.
	pal_special_on, pal_special_off procedures allow commands to
		control drc button etc on palette.
	Implemented coarse grid and lay_grid command

3/21/97 Max 1.1
	rmed dependence of Tcl/Tk install. 
	       (Tcl/Tk libs now looked for under $MMI_TOOLS/lib)

	Turned off ExtLength debugging :)

	Changed "length" extraction to put results in tcl var EXT_RES_SQUARES
	instead of in .ext file.
	
3/19/97 Max 1.0
	rmed dependence on Magic install.

	Now setup to allow different arch/os configurations to coexist
	in single installation. 

	Length extraction modified to give squares of resistance instead.

	Changed np in tsmc to a "lighter" diagonal pattern analagous to pp.

	All mmi tools under master directory.
		 pointed to by MMI_TOOLS environment variable.
		 install involves:
			1. obtaining license file!
			2. taring "mmi" directory to where you want it.
			3. setting MMI_TOOLS environment variable.
			4. putting appropraite bin/ in path, e.g.,
				$MMI_TOOLS/bin.sparc-solaris2 or
				$MMI_TOOLS/bin.i486-linux

	directory/file structure of max/ installation changed.
	
	System file search path now:  
		~/max_private
	 	$MMI_TOOLS/max_local
		$MMI_TOOLS/max<version>

	All tech related files now under tech/<techname> in system search path.
	Tech dependent names cleaned up:
		 tsmc.7bit.dstyle5 -> tsmc.display_styles
		 tsmc.7bit.cmap1   -> tsmc.color_map
		 tech_tsmc.tcl     -> tsmc.tcl
	Each technology now has own display_styles and color_map file.

	Support for tech variations.  If techname specified as "foo_bar" on
	command line.  Searchs for tech related files under 
	tech/foo/foo_bar.<whatever> first, and if not found then under
	tech/foo/foo.<whatever>.  Reads/writes max files of tech "foo"
	(Different tech variations share same max files).

	Code cleaned up quite a bit.
	Two modules: tech/ and wiring/, eliminated.

3/5/97 Max 0.42
	"-colormap new" message fixed :)
	license manager:
		augmented with "capabilities".
		made independent of max (so can be used in sue etc)
		cleaned up, and documented.
		license file moved to max_local

2/28/97 Max 0.41
	"max -colormap new" now works.
	focus problem on ":" command fixed.
	"extresis" no longer coredumps.
	":label" coredump problem fixed.
	new extractor warning option "dupglobal" controls whether warnings
	generated for same global label on distinct nodes.

2/18/97 Max 0.40
	converted to tk4.1

1/30/97 Max 0.39
	real R/C parms in extraction section of tsmc tech file.
	implemented 'ext_capacitance', gives total cap on selection

1/28/97 Max 0.38
	implemented: 'db_search paint <layers>'
	implemented: 'undo_disable' and 'undo_enable'
	
1/24/97 Max 0.37
	'sel_what labels' fixed to enumerate identical superposed
	labels in different cells.

1/14/97 Max 0.36
	readonly flag in list boxes
	window title now shows modified and readonly flags
	iconname fixed (now tracks window title)
	abort (Control-C) now does right thing for move, duplicate, zoom etc.
	labels don't get put on invisible layers (except for special cases
  		where a labels current layer connects to an invisible layer)
	Misc/See Cif menu elevated to toplevel menu ("Mask")
	Tools menu renamed "Tool" - attempt at consistency :)
	menu item removed:  
		Misc/Select Cells in Box 
	New Menu item (requested by David Murata):
		Misc/Box Dimensions
	While I was at it, I also added:
		Misc/Box Coordinates
	edit of not-yet-loaded instance works again.
	edit in-place now handles "load failure"
		(regular edit still doesn't do right thing on "load failure")	
	list boxes not cluttered up with "(UNNAMED)" cell, unless it has something
		in it!

1/10/97 Max 0.35
	labels now prefer to attach to visible layers!
	":feedback save" fixed. 
	now looks for tech_foo.tcl in lib/local before lib/
	Gets default tech from environment variable MAX_DEFAULT_TECH (if set)

1/8/97 Max 0.34
	subedit works again.
	always places box in window on load.
	handles "unavailable" buffers properly (allows load)
	doesn't write read-only files!
	doesn't warn when reading read-only files.
	can move duplicate with button 1 or 2
	panic save suffix changed from ".max.save.max" to ".max_panic_save"

1/6/97 Max 0.33
	busy cursor on undo/redo
	sel_what_cells - fixed coords.
	mode_abort (Cntl-C) now pops all the way to main mode.
	loss of focus problem solved 
		(e.g. when coming from list boxes with shift down)
	nwell in non-edit cell now easier to see.
	feedback display wierdness (solid bits) fixed.
	between command processing optimized (now ~ 6 milliseconds)
	preped for multiple bindings on commands.

1/5/97 Max 0.32
	new cell_path_add proc.

	cell path and file menu commands much improved (error checking, search
	path handling etc.) 
	
	modes modified to fix problem with undo (used to leave
	  stuff in wrong groups sometimes for instance).

	abort notification during gatekeeper calls (global variable
	  mode_abort is set during an abort).

	abort of wiring implemented.


